  "notes": "Paper constrains coupling of oscillating UDM to quarks and gluons (QCD sector) via molecular iodine spectroscopy, frequency range 10 Hz - 10^8 Hz (m ~ 4e-14 to 4e-7 eV). Main exclusion plot (Fig 3) is the combination QN\u00b7d = 0.999 d_gs + 0.092 d_mhat + ... which is a nucleon-mass-type scalar coupling, hence ScalarNucleon. Also reports bounds on d_alpha (ScalarPhoton, Fig 4a) and d_me (ScalarElectron, Fig 4b/5), so multiple couplings present. No numerical exclusion tables are provided; only plotted curves, so no reliable (mass, coupling) data points could be extracted. DM density assumed 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (galactic halo) plus solar/earth halo scenarios. Confidence reduced due to ambiguity among ScalarNucleon/ScalarPhoton/ScalarElectron and lack of tabulated data. | Vision: This plot is for d_me (ScalarElectron, electron mass variation), not ScalarNucleon as hinted. The lowest envelope of constraints over the full mass range is the Microscope (cyan) curve at low masses, but it rises steeply above ~3e-12 eV; at higher masses the lowest boundaries are the Be-Al/Be-Ti (brown/purple) solid lines. I traced the overall lower envelope of excluded region. Be-Cu, Cu-Pb, Cu-Pb alloy lines lie above. Coupling type is d_me; paper abstract emphasizes quark/gluon couplings but THIS figure constrains d_me specifically. | CV axis calibration succeeded (ranges consistent with LLM) | Curve traced by classical CV | Calibration: No calibration needed | Auto-corrected masses: 1/(eV\u2192MHz) i.e. MHz\u2192eV inverse (\u00d72.418e+08, rule=argmin|log10(median*f)-log10(anchor=1.0e-03)|) | Auto-corrected couplings: \u00d71e-20 (\u00d71.00e-20, rule=argmin|log10(median*f)-log10(anchor=1.0e-15)|)",
